===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|it|Malta}} or its source {{der|en|mt|Malta}}, from {{der|en|ar|مَالِطَا}}, {{m|ar|مَالِطَة}} (modern {{m|ar|مَالْطَا}}), from {{der|en|la|Melita}}, from {{der|en|grc|Μελίτη}}, which is disputed; from a {{der|en|phn|-}} root {{m|phn|𐤌𐤋𐤈}}, meaning "refuge" or from {{der|en|grc|μέλι|μέλι, μέλιτος|honey}}.  More at {{pedia|Malta#Etymology|Malta § Etymology|i=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɔːl.tə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɑl.tə/|/ˈmɔl.tə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Malta.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːltə|s=2}}

