==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{der|nl|la|Melita}}, from {{der|nl|grc|Μελίτη}}, which is disputed; from a {{der|nl|phn|-}} root {{m|phn|𐤌𐤋𐤈}}, meaning "refuge" or from {{der|nl|grc|μέλι|μέλι, μελίτος|honey}}.  More at {{w|Malta#Etymology|Malta}}.

The name of the neighbourhood is first attested as ''Maltha'' in 1641. It was named after the island in honour of the Battle of Malta of 1565.

